    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Tier 3 — Alchemist</strong></p><p><strong>“You can do it on purpose now. That’s worse.”</strong></p><p>By Tier 3, your body has adapted to your work. So has the world around you.</p><p>You understand instability not as danger, but as stored energy. You can touch volatile substances — physical or systemic — without flinching, and you know exactly how long you can keep your hands there.</p><p><strong>Tactical (Character Scale)</strong></p><ul><li>Gain resistance to <strong>acid</strong> and <strong>poison</strong> damage</li><li>You can identify the properties and risks of a strange substance within <strong>1 minute</strong></li><li>You reroll the lowest die on checks involving contamination, purification, or controlled degradation</li></ul><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li>During a Scenario involving toxic environments, industrial hazards, contamination cleanup, or unstable compounds, your faction gains <strong>Advantage</strong> on <strong>one</strong> relevant Opposed Strategic Roll</li></ul><p><strong>Cost:</strong> every hazard you normalize changes your threshold for “acceptable.” The line between mastery and acclimation gets thin.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
